## 2. Key findings

- **"Silent airport" is an announcement-policy label, not a physical-design outcome.** Schiphol, London City, Copenhagen, Helsinki-Vantaa, and Dubai all publicly describe themselves as silent or quiet. In every documented case, the operating change is that routine, general-terminal PA calls were stopped or moved to gate-only zones; the terminal itself was not re-clad in absorptive material as part of the announcement change. [Source: https://www.londoncityairport.com/at-the-airport/need-to-know/airport-policies/silent-policy] [Source: https://www.finavia.fi] [Source: https://media.dubaiairports.ae/dubai-international-gives-passengers-the-silent-treatment/]
- **The primary US regulatory anchor is NFPA 72, not FAA Part 139.** Part 139 §139.325 requires "a communications network" for the Airport Emergency Plan but sets no sound-pressure or intelligibility thresholds. NFPA 72 (adopted through local building codes) requires average STI ≥ 0.50 with no measurement point below 0.45 in required areas — the ceiling on how quiet a terminal can be without compromising life-safety intelligibility. [Source: https://www.suppressionsystems.com/voice-intelligibility-in-mass-notification-systems/]
- **The dominant PA/VA platforms in 2026 are IP-native.** Bosch PRAESENSA is deployed at Munich (10,000 zones, ~14,000 loudspeakers, described by Bosch as "the world's largest multi-subnet system") and Warsaw Chopin. IP-native systems make per-gate zoning and automated event-driven announcements a configuration decision rather than a wiring project — an important precondition for any "gate-only paging" policy. [Source: https://www.boschbuildingtechnologies.com/xc/en/stories/munich-airport-relies-on-a-networked-public-address-and-voice-alarm-solution/]
- **Automated multilingual announcements are commodity technology.** AviaVox — the phoneme-based synthetic-voice engine used by Schiphol and Heathrow — supports over 35 languages and integrates with major AODB / FIDS platforms. It is not a research project. [Source: https://aviavox.com/languages-and-scripts/languages/]
- **Directional / parametric-array loudspeakers exist but have thin airport track records.** Holosonics Audio Spotlight and comparable technologies (Genasys, formerly LRAD) are proven in retail and museum settings. Independent published airport deployments with measured spillover reductions are scarce; treat this layer as a targeted retrofit tool for specific problem zones, not as a baseline standard. [Source: https://www.holosonics.com/]
- **The most acute policy risk is digital exclusion.** A 2022 SITA survey found 26% of passengers used a mobile device for baggage-status updates (up from 14% in 2017) — meaning roughly three-quarters still relied on visual or audible channels. Silent-airport policies that assume near-universal app coverage disenfranchise the same populations MWAA's ADA and effective-communication obligations exist to protect. [Source: https://www.sita.aero/pressroom/news-releases/passenger-satisfaction-at-baggage-collection-jumps-to-a-new-high-with-mobile-notifications/]
- **The accessibility layer is now buildable off the shelf.** Frankfurt has trialed Bluetooth Auracast for direct-to-hearing-aid gate calls; MSP has deployed live speech-to-text captioning on gate monitors; SEA offers on-demand Video Remote Interpreting; ATL, PIT (Presley's Place, 1,500 sq ft, in Concourse A), and MSP operate purpose-built sensory rooms. These are commodity procurements in 2026, not moonshots. [Source: https://aerospaceglobalnews.com/news/frankfurt-airport-bluetooth-auracast-trial-accessibility/] [Source: https://metroairports.org/news/msp-airport-debuts-enhanced-accessibility-programs-travelers-who-are-deaf-hard-hearing] [Source: https://flypittsburgh.com/pittsburgh-international-airport/accessibility/sunflower-program/]
- **The muted-TV problem solved itself.** CNN Airport Network shut down on March 31, 2021, ending a 30-year presence on ~1,800 screens across 54 airports. The stated cause was that passengers had migrated to their phones. This is a rare piece of independent evidence that the passive-media layer of terminal audio has already collapsed under its own irrelevance. [Source: https://www.seattletimes.com/business/cnn-shutting-down-its-airport-network-after-nearly-30-years/]

