## 5. Cost signals (with honest caveats)

Independent cost data for airport PA/VA and acoustic packages at project-level detail is scarce; almost all figures below are directional.

- **PA/VA head-end and loudspeaker refresh.** General commercial PA benchmarks range from $5,000 to $75,000 for typical projects; airport-terminal deployments are orders of magnitude larger — Munich's Terminal 1 PRAESENSA install spans ~14,000 loudspeakers and 80+ rack cabinets. Public capital numbers are not disclosed. [Source: https://thenetworkinstallers.com/blog/pa-system-cost/]
- **Terminal construction as a denominator.** Recent US terminal builds average $50–$370 per square foot; the SFO Terminal 1 rebuild costs $1.36 billion. Against that denominator, the acoustic-and-communications package is a low-single-digit-percent line item — which is precisely the argument for specifying it before schematic design freezes. [Source: https://thecostguys.com/business/build-airport]
- **Off-the-shelf accessibility layer.** Sunflower lanyard programs, VRI service subscriptions, and Auracast trial hardware are procurement-scale items, not capital programs. Their marginal cost against the $9.0B (2024/2025 U&L) or $20–22.5B (July 2026 expansion) IAD envelope is negligible.

**Cost-data evidence gap.** I could not locate audited before/after cost or ROI figures for a "quiet-by-design" specification at any named peer. Vendor and consultant materials are not neutral. Any dollar figure quoted downstream of this brief should carry a source; if the source is a vendor, say so.

